.TH GRADEBOOK\-CODE 1 "2026-09" "gradebook" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
gradebook-code \- score a codebase against DRY, YAGNI, GRASP, SOLID and KISS
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B gradebook-code
.RI [ path ]
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Scores a codebase against the design principles it is usually only judged
against in review, and says which changes would move the score most.
.PP
The default path is the current directory.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-format " FORMAT"
.BR text ,
.B json
or
.B markdown
(default text).
.TP
.BI \-\-fail\-under " N"
Exit 1 when the score is below N. The CI gate.
.TP
.BI \-\-baseline " FILE"
A previous
.B "\-\-format json"
report to diff against.
.TP
.BR \-\-fail\-on\-drop " [\fIN\fR]"
With
.BR \-\-baseline ,
exit 1 when the score drops by more than N.
.TP
.B \-\-by\-dir
Also score each immediate subdirectory that holds code.
.TP
.BI \-\-top " N"
How many recommendations to show (default 5).
.TP
.BI \-\-max\-flags " N"
Cap the red flags listed (default all; 0 hides them).
.TP
.B \-\-list\-dimensions
Print the scoring model and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Scored, and no gate was breached.
.TP
.B 1
The score was below
.BR \-\-fail\-under ,
or dropped past
.BR \-\-fail\-on\-drop .
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Score this repository:
.PP
.RS
.B gradebook-code
.RE
.PP
Gate a pull request against the last score:
.PP
.RS
.B gradebook-code \-\-baseline last.json \-\-fail\-on\-drop 2
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR gradebook-tests (1).
Project documentation:
.UR https://github.com/fabiocicerchia/gradebook
.UE
